---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  Pagination shows the current item range on the start side and the page controls on the end side.
  The default <code>full</code> variant lists the first and last page, the current page and its
  neighbours, and fills the gaps with an ellipsis. It always uses the same number of slots, so the
  buttons do not shift while you move through pages.
</p>
<p>
  Listen to the <code>page</code> event; its detail is <code>{'{ page, pageSize }'}</code>. Changing the
  rows per page keeps the first visible item on screen instead of jumping back to page 1. Set
  <code>pageSizes</code> as a property to change the options.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-pagination style='width: 100%;' id='pagination-demo' page='5' page-size='10' total-items='240'></wc-pagination>

  <script is:inline>
    const paginationEl = document.getElementById('pagination-demo');
    paginationEl.pageSizes = [10, 25, 50, 100];
    paginationEl.addEventListener('page', event => {
      console.log('Pagination changed:', event.detail);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  On a narrow container the page list collapses to a <strong>Page [n] of N</strong> field and the
  rows-per-page label hides. The control is a <code>nav</code> landmark, the current page carries
  <code>aria-current="page"</code>, and range changes are announced to screen readers.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 22rem;'>
    <wc-pagination style='width: 100%;' page='5' page-size='10' total-items='240'></wc-pagination>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>
